WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.802
-Our first guest tonight
is an actor and comedian

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.871
you know best
from the "Jackass" franchise.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.472
New episodes from
his show "Reboot"

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.641
are available to stream
Tuesdays on Hulu.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.809
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:13.346
-Hey, Jared, you got a sec?
-Yeah, what's up?

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:16.849
-Uh, I'm in AA,
and I'm supposed to make amends

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.185
with people I might
have wronged, you know,

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.687
back when I was overdoing it?

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.022
-Must be a hell of a list.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.657
And since you're here,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.492
thought I might as well
pop my cherry with you.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:31.197
-Yeah, okay.
I'll try to be gentle.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.365
-Back then,
I either came to work drunk,

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.667
stoned, or hung over.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.470
I can't even remember
Season Three. [ Chuckles ]

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.739
But shouldn't have done it.
Filled with regrets.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:43.175
Uh, blah, blah, blah.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:47.046
-Well, Clay, thanks
for those heartfelt words.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:52.218
-Good.
-Okay, boys! Take him up!

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.886
-Please welcome to the show,

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:56.022
our friend, Johnny Knoxville,
everybody!

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:59.058
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:03.963 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:08.868 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.871
-Hello!
-Hello!

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.373
-I'm really happy
to have you here.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:16.376
I was also really happy to
hear you on the wonderful

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.145
Dana Carvey,
David Spade podcast.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.280
You came clean about
something you did to me

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.648
when you hosted "SNL" in 2005.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.850
-Accidentally did to you.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.420
-I do not --
We have video proof here.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.888
-Okay, let's --
-First, I want to show this.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.056
This is your monologue.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.724
I want to show people
how it was written.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.027
This is how it was written
for the actual night.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:38.297
It goes, "Seth comes on stage,
tackles Johnny, and then --"

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:40.432 line:0%
Sorry, here's where it is.
This is the important thing.

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:42.001 line:0%
"System of a Down is here,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.869 line:0%
so stick around,
we'll be right back.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:48.240 line:0%
Then Seth hits
Johnny in the nuts."

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.477 line:0%
That's how it was scripted.
-That's how it was scripted.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:55.448
And I never got a chance
to apologize to you

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.284
on national TV
for misreading the card.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.652
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:02.488
-So that's the accident, is
you misread Wally's cards?

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.523
-Yes, I got the words -- Yeah.

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.526
-Okay, because I think you'll
see by watching this clip

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.194
that it also
caught me off guard.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.462
Let's take a look.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.430
-There you have it.
That's how my week has been.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.698
I'm not complaining.

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:14.466
I'm hosting
"Saturday Night Live."

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:15.835
We got a great show --

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.169
Oh!

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.604
Great show tonight, yeah!
-Yeah.

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.206
-System of a Down is here.
-Oh!

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.741
-Stick around,
we'll be right back!

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.177
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.781
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.517
-I'm laughing,
but I'm hurting inside.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.918
Because I did not mean
to do that.

00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:35.288
-Well, I hadn't watched
that clip since then.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.923
And when I watched it,
I hurt inside.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.959
-It was a solid shot.
-It was a real solid shot.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.394
-I don't want to get graphic,

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:46.031
but I felt the whole outline of
your business on my hand.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:48.400
And, you know --
-Yeah.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.236
-He's packing some lumber.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.672
-Yeah, I will say, I really --
when I fell down,

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:55.708
I both felt intense pain,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.444
but I will say, part of my brain
thought, "He's one of the best."

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.478
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.080
He's one of the best
that ever did it.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.082
-We had to go right into
the next scene, though.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.251
-Yeah.
-You were in such pain.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.219
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.854
I felt almost terrible.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.055
-You were really
torn up about it.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.623
Congratulations.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.558
So this is a very novel take

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.627
on a phenomenon that's been
happening a lot

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:18.564
in the last decade-plus, about
rebooting classic sitcoms.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.132
But this is
a really cool take on it.

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:26.172
How would you explain "Reboot?"
-Well, it's a show about a show.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.775
The main characters,
we all get a chance --

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.910
we didn't get along
when we first made the show.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.113
It was like a "Family Ties" type
of -- not "Family Ties."

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.116
-Like, "Family Matters."
-A "Full House" type of show.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:41.054
And then we get a chance 15
years later to remake the show.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:46.859
And we all have our things,
our obstacles.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.662
Picture this --
I play a naughty comedian

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.129
who has overdone it in his past.

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:52.264
-[ Laughter ] Uh-huh?

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:53.733
-Maybe drank a little
too much at times.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.834
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.202
A stretch, as it's known
in the acting biz.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.203
-A stretch.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.337
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:01.106
But I'm just trying to
do the best I can.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:02.341
Like,
every character on the show

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:04.143
is trying to do
the best they can,

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.911
but we kind of get in
our own ways.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:09.214
-I was mentioning this,
Steve-O was here recently,

00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:11.717
and I was talking about
the last "Jackass" movie.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.220
It affected me in a way
that I didn't think it would.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.826
I thought it was really funny,
but I also, I felt nostalgic.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:22.228
It was genuinely emotional
to see so many of you

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.696
still doing it
all these years later.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.330
Does it feel that way
when you're together?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.299
-First of all, thank you.

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:31.770
And yeah, it does feel pretty
wonderful when we're together.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.341
I mean, it's nerve-racking
and a lot of things.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:38.110
But I mean, we've been
friends for 20 years,

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:43.215
and we created something that
grew into whatever it is.

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:46.586
And yeah. It's special.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:49.488
-It's cool to -- I mean, nothing
sort of endures that long.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:52.190
I think it reminds
a lot of people about

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.061
their friend groups, which are
sort of lovingly idiotic.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.262
-Yeah.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.131
-And that comes across
all the time.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.800
-Sure, everyone did
silly things like this

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.768
growing up with their friends.

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:04.437
-We just didn't think
to monetize it.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.372
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.773
-Yeah.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:10.977
-I know you've got kids.
You've got some younger kids.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.478
Do they find their way
to "Jackass?"

00:05:13.478 --> 00:05:16.148
When do they -- I can't imagine
you show to it them.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.518
-Okay, no.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.452
Their friends have seen it.
-Right.

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:21.920
-And I think out of
their friend group,

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.090
my kids have seen it the least.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.626
Like, I'll show them,
as far as I know,

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.294
I'll show them a bit
here and there.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.595
But nothing naughty,

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.998
or nothing where Daddy gets
knocked out, you know?

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.365
-Yeah.

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:37.170
-So my oldest daughter,
she was 14 when I let her

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.704
go to the "Jackass 3D" premiere,

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.139
and she had to sit
right next to me.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:43.109
And I'm like, "Baby, you have to
close your eyes at some parts,

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:46.946
close your ears in others,
and close both in..." you know?

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.013
And she did.

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:49.815
-She did?
-Yeah.

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:53.085
And plus, my son is --
The girls are smart, right?

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:56.589
And Rocco's smart, but he's,
like, a little excitable.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:59.058
-Yeah.
-And he wants to do that stuff,

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.226
and I let him know that's
not really going to happen.

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:02.961
-I mean, I can't imagine.

00:06:02.961 --> 00:06:04.263
Because I'm always
telling my kids,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.464
"Don't do that. It's dangerous."

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.466
But I got to imagine it's
so empty coming from you.

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.269
-No, no, no --
Well, okay, that's fair.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.937
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.573
If they crack
a joke or something,

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:17.944
if it's a little on the line,
I'm like, "That's alright."

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:19.045
-Yeah.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.079
-But I remember when they
were real little,

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.714
I was a helicopter parent.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.149
-Yeah.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:25.117
-At the playground, because
I don't want them to get hurt.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:28.087
-Yeah, I would imagine, right.
-I was -- yeah.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.489
I don't know if
it makes sense, but --

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:30.589
-I think it does make sense.

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.291
Certainly, you know
the repercussions.

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:36.696
I would just say, I hope that
they don't make the mistake

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:37.797
that I made, and trust you.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.733
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.501
-God forbid they trust
their father.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.903
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:46.138
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.506
-Thank you.

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.275
-It is always such a delight
to see you, old friend.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.409
Johnny Knoxville!

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.077
New episodes of "Reboot"
available to stream

00:06:52.077 --> 00:06:53.146
Tuesdays on Hulu.

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.414
We'll be right back
with Jake Lacy.

